#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/project.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Project lifecycle and tasks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:69
msgid ""
"When a project reaches a terminal state or is deleted, task handling is "
"explicit:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Event                | Task behavior (v1 default)                                                                                                                                                                         |\n"
"| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `status → completed` | Prompt: bulk move pending tasks back to Backlog / bulk complete / keep in project. **Default: move back to Backlog** (`project_id` cleared, `milestone_id` cleared, restore `list_id` if retained) |\n"
"| `status → cancelled` | Same as `completed`                                                                                                                                                                                |\n"
"| `status → on_hold`   | Tasks **keep** `project_id`; project UI read-only or degraded edit                                                                                                                                 |\n"
"| Delete project       | All tasks move back to Backlog (not deleted); milestone entities deleted or orphaned per cascade rules                                                                                             |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:78
msgid ""
"Project archive semantics use **`project.status`** (and optional future "
"`archived_at`) — **do not** reuse `task_list.body.closed`. Task-list archive "
"(`closed: true`) remains: sidebar hidden, **mutations forbidden** (`清单已归"
"档`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "**[v2+]** Archived project context marks weak reference chains; file co-archive is user-explicit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/project.md:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contents inside a project"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:88
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Type              | Description                                  | Ownership                                           |\n"
"| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Task              | Smallest execution unit; pending / completed | Belongs to project when `body.project_id` is set    |\n"
"| Project materials | Files/docs not tied to a task                | **[v2+]** — file entity + project reference         |\n"
"| Linked entities   | Diary, notes, clips                          | **[v2+]** — weak refs via future relationship layer |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/features/project.md:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backlog / task module (`/tasks`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:94
msgid ""
"The **task module** is the existing `/tasks` Shell route: multiple "
"`task_list`s, folder tree, Smart Lists, and archived lists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Rule          | Detail                                                                                                                                                      |\n"
"| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Scope         | \"Not in any project\" means `task_item.body.project_id` is **null**                                                                                          |\n"
"| Multi-list    | Unassigned tasks may live in **any** normal list (including the default list `is_default`, e.g. Inbox) — not a single Backlog list                          |\n"
"| Visibility    | Tasks with `project_id` set are **hidden** from task-module list views                                                                                      |\n"
"| Default list  | The lazy-created default list remains a normal list inside the task module — it is **not** a sync inbox between task module and projects                    |\n"
"| No sync inbox | There is **no** auto two-way sync or \"inbox\" that requires tidying on both sides. Tasks belong to **either** the task module **or** a project at any moment |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:104
msgid ""
"Smart Lists and archived lists follow the same module; see [Smart Lists]"
"(#smart-lists)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/features/project.md:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "Task ownership (task module ↔ project)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/project.md:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "Core rule"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:112
msgid ""
"A task belongs to **one side at a time**: either the task module (Backlog) "
"**or** exactly one project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Action                                 | Effect                                                                                                                            |\n"
"| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Drag task from Backlog into project    | Set `project_id`; task disappears from task-module views                                                                          |\n"
"| Move task from project back to Backlog | Clear `project_id` (and `milestone_id`); task reappears in task module                                                            |\n"
"| Move task project A → project B        | Direct transfer; **clear `milestone_id`** (milestones are project-scoped)                                                         |\n"
"| Global search                          | Matches all tasks; result shows归属 `Backlog / {list name}` or `Project / {project title}`; click navigates to the owning surface |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/features/project.md:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data model (extensions to `task_item`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/features/project.md:127
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Field          | Type             | Rule                                                                                                                                                                                |\n"
"| -------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `list_id`      | `number`         | Required for tasks in Backlog. When in a project: **retain last list id** (recommended) so move-back restores position; alternatively null and restore to default list on move-back |\n"
"| `project_id`   | `number \\| null` | Set when task is in a project; null when in Backlog                                                                                                                                 |\n"
"| `milestone_id` | `number \\| null` | Optional; must reference a milestone in the **same** project; cleared on cross-project move or move back to Backlog                                                                 |\n"
msgstr ""

